  "title": "Volatility adjusted yield: option yield per unit of risk",
  "summary": "The key question for an option seller: am I paid enough for the risk? The speaker's VAY metric divides option yield by risk. For a one-month at-the-money covered call, a VAY of 0.5 means 0.5 units of yield per unit of risk, a poor trade; 2.2 is a good trade. Two trades with the same premium can have very different VAY.",
